# SEP490 Children's Toy Admin FE – Cursor Rules

# ============================================================
# MANDATORY: Read CODING_RULES.md before any code change
# ============================================================

<rule>
You MUST read the file `CODING_RULES.md` at the project root before writing
or modifying any code in this project. It contains 24 sections covering:
folder structure, naming conventions, component rules, hooks, data fetching,
axios client, state management, loading/error/empty states, optimistic updates,
styling, TypeScript, performance, environment variables, build config,
deployment, git workflow, anti-patterns, code style, security, CI/CD,
validation, error handling, accessibility, and dependency management.

Do NOT skip this step. The rules are project-specific and override general
best practices you may know.
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Project Stack
# ============================================================

<rule>
Stack:
- Framework: Next.js 16 with App Router
- UI Library: React 19
- Language: TypeScript 5 (strict mode ON)
- Styling: TailwindCSS 4 + tailwind-merge
- HTTP Client: Axios (via @/configs/axios-client ONLY)
- Forms: React Hook Form + Zod + @hookform/resolvers
- Font: Outfit (next/font/google)

Code comments and UI text: Vietnamese
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Folder Structure (strict)
# ============================================================

<rule>
Always place new code in the correct folder:

src/features/<feature>/
  components/   → UI components for this feature
  hooks/        → Custom hooks (useFeature.ts, useFeatureMutations.ts)
  services/     → API calls (<feature>-api.ts)
  types/        → TypeScript interfaces + Zod schemas (<feature>.schema.ts)

src/components/ → Shared UI components
src/hooks/      → Shared custom hooks
src/configs/    → Configuration files (axios-client.ts)
src/context/    → React Context (only: theme, sidebar, auth)
src/types/      → Shared TypeScript types

NEVER import directly between features. Use src/hooks/ or src/components/ for shared logic.
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Server vs Client Components
# ============================================================

<rule>
Default = Server Component (no directive needed).

Add "use client" ONLY when:
- Using useState, useEffect, useReducer
- Handling events (onClick, onChange)
- Accessing browser APIs (localStorage, window)
- Using Context

NEVER add "use client" to:
- app/(admin)/layout.tsx
- app/layout.tsx
- Any page.tsx unless truly necessary

Push "use client" as deep (leaf) as possible.
</rule>

# ============================================================
# TypeScript
# ============================================================

<rule>
- strict: true – NEVER use `any`. Use `unknown` if type is unclear.
- Infer types from Zod schemas: `export type Foo = z.infer<typeof FooSchema>`
  Do NOT write duplicate TypeScript interfaces that mirror Zod schemas.
- All component props must have explicit TypeScript interface.
- Prefer named exports for feature components; default export only for page.tsx and layout.tsx.
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Axios – Strict Rule
# ============================================================

<rule>
NEVER import axios directly:
  ❌ import axios from "axios";

ALWAYS use the shared axios instance:
  ✅ import axiosClient from "@/configs/axios-client";

All API calls must go through src/features/<feature>/services/<feature>-api.ts
Never call axiosClient directly from a component or hook.
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Custom Hooks
# ============================================================

<rule>
Hooks must:
1. Return an OBJECT (not tuple): return { data, isLoading, error, create }
2. Include loading + error state
3. Have cleanup in useEffect that fetches data:
   useEffect(() => {
     let cancelled = false;
     fetch().then(d => { if (!cancelled) setData(d); });
     return () => { cancelled = true; };
   }, []);

If hook > 80 lines: split into useFeature (query) + useFeatureMutations (mutation).
</rule>

# ============================================================
# useCallback / useMemo / React.memo
# ============================================================

<rule>
useCallback: ONLY use when the receiving child component is wrapped in React.memo().
  Without React.memo() on child, useCallback has NO effect on re-renders.

useMemo: Use for expensive computations, derived data (filter, sort, paginate).
  Do NOT use for simple value transforms.

React.memo(): Use selectively for components that re-render unnecessarily.
  Verify with React DevTools Profiler before applying.

These three MUST work together:
  const MemoChild = React.memo(ChildComponent);
  const handler = useCallback(() => doSomething(), [dep]);
  <MemoChild onAction={handler} />
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Forms & Validation
# ============================================================

<rule>
Every form MUST:
1. Have a Zod schema in features/<feature>/types/<feature>.schema.ts
2. Use React Hook Form with zodResolver
3. Show inline validation errors (in Vietnamese)
4. Have submit button disabled={isSubmitting} with loading indicator
5. Map server 400 validation errors to form fields using setError:

   if (status === 400 && response.data?.errors) {
     Object.entries(response.data.errors).forEach(([field, msgs]) => {
       setError(field, { type: "server", message: msgs[0] });
     });
   }
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Loading / Error / Empty States
# ============================================================

<rule>
Every component that renders data from an API MUST handle all 4 states:
1. isLoading → <Skeleton /> or <Spinner />
2. error → <ErrorState message={error} />
3. data.length === 0 → <EmptyState />
4. data → render content

NEVER leave the UI blank during loading or after an error.

Submit buttons must reflect isSubmitting:
  <button disabled={isSubmitting}>
    {isSubmitting ? <><Spinner /> Đang lưu...</> : "Lưu"}
  </button>
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Error Handling
# ============================================================

<rule>
NEVER leave catch{} empty.
NEVER use catch only for console.log without user feedback.

Pattern:
  try {
    await api.create(data);
    toast.success("Tạo thành công");
  } catch (error) {
    toast.error(error instanceof Error ? error.message : "Có lỗi xảy ra");
    if (process.env.NODE_ENV === "development") {
      console.error("[context]", error);
    }
  }

HTTP status handling (in axios-client.ts interceptor):
  401 → xóa token, redirect /login
  403 → toast "Không có quyền"
  404 → toast "Không tìm thấy"
  500 → toast "Lỗi server"
  network → toast "Mất kết nối"
</rule>

# ============================================================
# List Rendering
# ============================================================

<rule>
NEVER use key={index} for list items.
ALWAYS use key={item.id} (unique ID from data).

Reason: index as key causes bugs when list order changes (items lose their state).
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Accessibility Baseline
# ============================================================

<rule>
Minimum a11y requirements:
- Icon-only buttons MUST have aria-label: <button aria-label="Xóa tài khoản">
- Inputs MUST have associated label: <label htmlFor="x"><input id="x" />
- Modals MUST have role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby
- Use <button>, not <div> or <span>, for interactive elements
- disabled button: add aria-disabled={true} alongside disabled
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Dependencies
# ============================================================

<rule>
Before suggesting or installing ANY new npm package:
1. Check /docs/dependencies.md – is there already a package for this?
2. Check bundle size on bundlephobia.com
3. If adding: update /docs/dependencies.md with package info before merging

NEVER add a package without registering it in /docs/dependencies.md.
</rule>

# ============================================================
# Code Quality
# ============================================================

<rule>
- No console.log in production code (wrap in NODE_ENV === "development")
- No hardcoded URLs or API keys (use process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL)
- No component over 150 lines without splitting
- No nested if/for deeper than 3 levels
- Commit messages: Conventional Commits (feat:, fix:, refactor:, chore:, docs:)
- Branch naming: feature/, fix/, chore/, refactor/
</rule>
